      "problem": "$\\frac{1}{8}÷4=$",
      "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $4$ is $\\frac{1}{4}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{8}\\,÷\\,4=\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{8}\\times \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1\\times 1}{8\\times 4}=\\frac{1}{32}\n$$",
